WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.502
-Can I ask you to tell the story

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:05.038
that you told about
"Bon Appetit" magazine?

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:09.241
-This is about you.
I'm here to talk about you.

00:00:09.241 --> 00:00:11.811
-So the "Bon Appetit" magazine
is in my new special,

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:13.313
"The Old Man and the Pool."

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:15.014
No, it's --
can you tell that story

00:00:15.014 --> 00:00:16.316
or you don't want to
tell that story?

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:18.784
-Sure, I can tell it.
I mean, it's a long story.

00:00:18.784 --> 00:00:20.286
We'll have to probably
cut it out of the show.

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:21.387
I don't know, but...

00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:23.122
I was just telling this
story that --

00:00:23.122 --> 00:00:24.523
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.523 --> 00:00:26.626
-I love this story. If they
cut it out, they cut it out.

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:29.595
-My mom was
a very, very funny person,

00:00:29.595 --> 00:00:34.434
and always, she would call me up
and she would say something

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:35.969
to either annoy me
or something like that.

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:37.536
And I'd go, "All right, Mom,
I can't take it anymore.

00:00:37.536 --> 00:00:38.972
I've got to hang up."

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:40.240
She'd be like, "Don't hang up.
Wait, wait. One more thing."

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:43.376
So I called her once,
I said, "Hey, Mom,"

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:45.278
I go,
"'Bon Appetit' magazine called.

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:47.647
For Mother's Day,
they're doing a special issue

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:49.515
and they want to know if you
have any recipes maybe."

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:54.154
She goes, "Oh, my God.
'Bon Appetit' magazine.

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:55.555
Oh, my --

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.257
I'm going to be
in 'Bon Appetit' magazine?

00:00:57.257 --> 00:00:59.859
Oh, my God. I don't know
what I'm going to do.

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:02.094
Maybe my shrimp recipe?"
I go, "Whatever."

00:01:02.094 --> 00:01:03.162
I go, "Think about it.

00:01:03.162 --> 00:01:04.163
Call me tomorrow
and let me know."

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:05.464
And she said, "Okay."

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:06.866
So I get the phone call
the next day and she goes,

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:09.335
"I got the recipe
that I'm going to give.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.171
It's my cheesecake recipe."

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:13.939
I go, "Okay, great, I love it.
Well, can you send it over?"

00:01:13.939 --> 00:01:15.608
She's like, "Yeah,
Daddy's going to type it,

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.010
because you know, he knows
how to use the computer."

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.879
So my Dad,
"I'll type the thing."

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:22.048
So he types out the thing,
makes a big deal.

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:24.851
-That's a really funny
impersonation of your dad.

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:28.387
-He loves it. He loves it.
-[ Groans ]

00:01:28.387 --> 00:01:29.722
Cruel. Cruel.

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:32.892
-So he emails it to me,
and so I get the thing,

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:34.561
and so I give it
to 'Bon Appetit' magazine,

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:35.862
emailed to them.

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:37.730
They go,
"Alright, Jimmy, thank you.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:38.865
Thank your mom so much."

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:41.067
You know, we have to
make this recipe

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:44.237
to make sure it's good.

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:45.604
Sure. Of course.

00:01:45.604 --> 00:01:47.640
Do whatever you guys got to do.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.642
So they call back the next day
and they go,

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:53.946
"We made your mom's recipe
and it's fantastic.

00:01:53.946 --> 00:01:55.148
It's really good."
[ Crowd awws ]

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:56.649
I go,
"Okay, cool, I love it."

00:01:56.649 --> 00:02:00.085
"Can you ask her,
is there a story behind it?

00:02:00.085 --> 00:02:01.654
You know, did she get it
from Grandma or somebody?"

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:02.855
Is there
something behind this?"

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:03.856
I go, "Absolutely."

00:02:03.856 --> 00:02:05.358
So I call my mom.
She goes, "Hello?"

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:06.358
I go, "Bon Appetit' loves it."

00:02:06.358 --> 00:02:07.426
She's like, "Oh, my God.

00:02:07.426 --> 00:02:09.328
I'm going to be
in 'Bon Appetit.'"

00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:11.698
I go, "They want to know,
is there a story behind it?"

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:13.266
Is it Grandma's?

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:14.901
What's the story
behind the recipe?"

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:15.935
She goes,
"Hold on a second."

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:17.169
And she puts the phone
on the chair

00:02:17.169 --> 00:02:19.405
and I can hear her
scuffling over to the thing,

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:22.408
and I hear she opens up
the cupboard,

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:25.911
and then I hear paper, like --

00:02:25.911 --> 00:02:27.146
And she goes, "Yeah.

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:30.716
I got it from
'Bon Appetit' magazine."

00:02:30.716 --> 00:02:32.619
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:33.686
[ Rimshot ]

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:36.322
-Great story.
-"I'm hanging up."

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.591
"I'm hanging up the phone.
I've had enough."

